  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Georgia Mail**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **Last Train to Clarksville**: back after 116 archived shows (457 days) [4]\n- **White Freightliner**: rare: 7 archived performances [4]\n- **Bird Song**: rare: 12 archived performances [4]\n- **Letter to Seymour**: rare: 11 archived performances [4]\n- **Believe**: rare: 9 archived performances [4]\n- **Blue Mule**: rare: 14 archived performances [4]\n- **She Makes My Love Come Rolling Down**: rare: 14 archived performances [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2019-09-01.AT822.flac24** (recommended): source not stated; 24 songs; 131 min [1]\n- **billystrings2019-09-01.skm140.flac16**: source not stated; 17 songs; 118 min [2]. Said about its sound: Recording begins halfway through the first song, because the taper arrived as the band started playing [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Taper's first time running this rig in almost four years; Russ Minas provided clamp space [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2019-09-01.AT822.flac24**: taped by Russ Minas; transferred by Russ Minas; source: FOB Audio-Technica AT822 (12') > Zoom H4n [1]. Also: Chain: AT822 at 12 feet, into a Zoom H4n, edited in Audacity, saved as 24-bit/96 FLAC [1]\n- **billystrings2019-09-01.skm140.flac16**: taped by John Fairbairn; transferred by John Fairbairn; source: Neumann skm140(50' from stage/7' high/DFC/[X/Y]) > Sound Devices MixPre > Olympus LS-10(24/48) [2]\n\n## Art and photos\n\n- Poster by @BillybaseDotNet: [Billy Strings Howelsen Hill - BillyBase](https://billybase.net/venue/howelsen-hill/) [5]",
